        "id": "observation-14",
        "status": "final",
        "code": {
          "text": "Skin examination"
        },
        "subject": {
          "reference": "Patient/patient-1"
        },
        "valueString": "Ill-defined hypopigmented macules and patches on both cheeks and lateral jaw, 1–3 cm, with very fine scale on close inspection and borders not sharply demarcated; background mildly tanned, with no complete depigmentation or erythema. A few faint hypopigmented patches with minimal scale on upper arms. Trunk clear, with no lesions described as consistent with tinea versicolor and no classic chalk-white vitiligo patches."
      }
